 ],
 "notes": "DeletionPolicy Retain on the launch and use roles is unchecked: verified in normalize_cfn that DeletionPolicy is exposed only on instantiated resources (__resource__), and __declared__ carries Properties only, so a correct template (both roles off by default) never shows it; extending declared() would make it checkable. Role checks use __declared__ because every role is condition-gated. The eight service roles are matched by trust principal, not name. Unquoted YES/NO decode to booleans, so true/false are accepted as defaults. That decoding also makes the adapter evaluate such a template's conditions false, so its roles and outputs disappear from the real view: outputs_role_arns (min 9, because launch and use outputs are condition-gated) and launch_use_off_by_default are detail for that reason and because outputs are detail per C9. The eight service-role policy checks are detail because the prompt names no policies; they only require an AWS-managed ARN naming the service. Service-role existence is core. Inline permissions accept a separate AWS::IAM::Policy attached to the use role. Review 2026-11-10: roles_session also accepts every role omitting MaxSessionDuration (the IAM default is one hour); separate AWS::IAM::RolePolicy is accepted as the use role's inline policy."
}
